  "answer_text": "Depending on what you are looking for, **\"iCloud Control\"** typically refers to one of three things:\n\n---\n\n### 1. iCloud for Windows (Formerly \"iCloud Control Panel\")\nIf you are looking for Apple\u2019s official software to sync and control your iCloud data on a Windows PC, it is now officially called **iCloud for Windows**.\n* **What it does:** It lets you sync your iCloud Photos (into the Windows Photos app), access iCloud Drive files directly through File Explorer, autofill passwords using iCloud Passwords, and sync your iCloud Contacts, Calendars, and Bookmarks.\n* **How to get it:** You can download it directly from the **Microsoft Store** on Windows 10 or 11.\n\n---\n\n### 2. \"iCloud Control\" Mac Utility (Third-Party App)\nIf you are looking for the open-source Mac utility named **iCloud Control**, it is a tool designed to give macOS users selective synchronization power over iCloud Drive.\n* **What it does:** Normally, macOS manages what gets kept locally and what is offloaded to the cloud automatically. This utility adds a menu/extension to Finder so you can manually force files or entire folders to stay downloaded locally or remain strictly in the cloud to save space.\n* **How to get it:** You can download it via GitHub (by developer *Obbut* or *Njmcq*) or install it using Homebrew by running the following command in Terminal:\n  ```bash\n  brew install --cask icloud-control\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### 3. General iCloud Settings (Managing Storage & Syncing)\nIf you simply want to manage, control, or limit your iCloud storage usage, backups, and app synchronization, you can do so directly from your device's settings:\n\n* **On iPhone or iPad:** Go to **Settings** > **[Your Name]** > **iCloud**. Here you can turn sync on/off for specific apps (Photos, Contacts, Notes, etc.) and select *Manage Account Storage* to delete old backups or upgrade your storage plan.\n* **On a Mac:** Go to the **Apple menu (\uf8ff)** > **System Settings** > click your **Apple Account** (at the top) > **iCloud**. \n* **On any device (via Web Browser):** Log in to **[iCloud.com](https://www.icloud.com)** to view and manage your files, photos, emails, and account settings directly from the web.",
